    "q-143511": {
      "dom_id": "step-q143511",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "| $x$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $0.3$ | $0.5$ | $0.1$ | $0.1$ |\n\nLet ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{80}$ be a random sample of size $n=80$ from a population with the probability mass function given above. Find an approximation for the probability that the sample mean is greater than $0.1.$\n\n*Note: $Φ(z)$ is the cumulative distribution function for the standard normal distribution.*",
      "worked_solution": "Suppose that ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{n}$ is a random sample of size $n$ from a population with population mean $\\mu $ and population standard deviation $\\sigma .$ The central limit theorem (or CLT) states that for sufficiently large $n,$ the distribution of the sample mean $\\overset{―}{X}$ can be approximated as \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{X}∼N\\,(\\mu ,\\frac{{\\sigma }^{2}}{n}).\n$$\n\nIn our case:\n\n- the sample size is \n\n$$\nn=80,\n$$\n\n- the population mean is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mu  & =\\text{E}[X] \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}f({x}_{i}) \\\\  & =-1\\cdot 0.3+0\\cdot 0.5+1\\cdot 0.1+2\\cdot 0.1 \\\\  & =-0.3+0+0.1+0.3 \\\\  & =0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- the population variance is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }^{2} & =\\text{Var}[X] \\\\  & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2} \\\\  & =((-1)^{2}\\cdot 0.3+{0}^{2}\\cdot 0.5+{1}^{2}\\cdot 0.1+{2}^{2}\\cdot 0.1)-{0}^{2} \\\\  & =(0.3+0+0.1+0.4)-0 \\\\  & =0.8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by the CLT, we have that the distribution of the sample mean can be approximated as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{X} & ∼N\\,(\\mu ,\\frac{{\\sigma }^{2}}{n}) \\\\  & ∼N\\,(0,\\frac{0.8}{80}) \\\\  & ∼N(0,0.01).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe want to find $P(\\overset{―}{X}>0.1).$ So, we convert $\\overset{―}{X}$ to a standard normal random variable by $z$-scoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(\\overset{―}{X}>0.1) & ≈P(Z>\\frac{0.1-0}{\\sqrt{0.01}}) \\\\  & =P(Z>1) \\\\  & =1-Φ(1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\nP(\\overset{―}{X}>0.1)=1-Φ(1).\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
